  "interpretation": [
    "The six visibility edit workloads improve in every one of the 108 native pairs, with matching outputs and a measured drop from 3 raw-tree builds to 1 in every diagnostic cell.",
    "Controls are mixed. The 1,000-file search control records a 22.224786 percent paired median reduction with 5 of 6 favorable pairs and a wide pair range. Both variants build the tree and visibility once; the recorded change cannot be attributed to avoided tree rebuilds.",
    "The 1,000-file search result includes a retained extreme baseline observation, but the cause is unproven and the measured improvement must not be dismissed as established noise.",
    "Other control medians span slowdowns and speedups: no across-the-board search, preview, initial-load or sort improvement is established.",
    "These are synthetic one-folder component timings around awaited projection calls. Fixture construction, recognition, receipt generation, diagnostics, compilation and filesystem scanning are outside the timer. Cold means a new filter actor in an already initialized process.",
    "The release benchmark uses an isolated library with testability enabled in both variants. It does not measure whole-player frame rate, CPU, memory, energy or end-to-end UI latency.",
    "Keep this complete native cohort separate from historical incomplete Linux data and failed native packaging attempt 1."
  ],
